  "improves": "a change improves BASE only if it nets more in EVERY year, its fall is at most 1 point above BASE's in every year, it makes at least 40 trades in every year, and the paired weekly difference from BASE has t >= 2",
  "safer": "a change is safer if its fall in BASE's worst year is at least 2 points lower, its worst year's net is not below BASE's worst year, and its three-year net is at least 90% of BASE's. Reported separately; it trades money for safety, and the owner chooses",
  "selection_luck": "for each year held out: among BASE and all variants with falls <= 25% and 40+ trades in the other two, take the highest worse-of-two net, and score it on the held-out year against BASE. If this does not beat BASE in all three, choosing among these variants is not shown to help",
  "lots": "the lot-limit answer: the highest three-year net among LOTS|1,2,3,5 and BASE with every year's fall <= 15%",
  "final": "FINAL = BASE plus every change that improves. If two or more improve, their combination is replayed and must itself improve on BASE; each improving change is also applied to the 20 random-entry books and reported. If none improves, FINAL = BASE",
  "correctness": "analyze_r.check_book on every replay; a variant with trades identical to BASE is reported as no effect",
  "status": "NIFTY 2024, 2025 and Jan - Oct 2026 are all seen. A pass is a candidate for real fills and the forward panels, never proof. Nothing in the system changes on this; the owner decides."
